  "title": "idl2wrs: Fix format-truncation warning",
  "description": "Just allocate space for the hfvalsstring on demand, since we\nonly use it once. It adds 6 bytes to the generated valstring,\nso not using the same buffer size prevents the gcc warning:\n\n```c\nwireshark/epan/dissectors/dcerpc/idl2wrs.c:2961:56: warning: ‘%s’ directive output may be truncated writing up to 255 bytes into a region of size 251 [-Wformat-truncation=]\n 2961 |         snprintf(hfvalsstring, BASE_BUFFER_SIZE, \"VALS(%s)\", valsstring);\n      |                                                        ^~    ~~~~~~~~~~\nwireshark/epan/dissectors/dcerpc/idl2wrs.c:2961:9: note: ‘snprintf’ output between 7 and 262 bytes into a destination of size 256\n 2961 |         snprintf(hfvalsstring, BASE_BUFFER_SIZE, \"VALS(%s)\", valsstring);\n      |         ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n```\n\nPing #20175",
  "state": "merged",
